  "changelog": [
    {
      "item": "B",
      "change": "One-shot arming (the blocker of all three S8.4 reviews): U12 flip-flop A = STARTED latch (PRE_N = START_N = NAND(MAIN_LED_OK, RUN) on the spare U14 gate 2, CLR_N = RESET_N, CLK = GND); TIMER_GO = RUN AND STARTED; the U11 output IS ARMED (R71); TP19 = STARTED. R83 200k -> 120k: V20_OK 9.06-10.96 V, a U5 status-validity floor (>= 3.56 V above vSafe5V max, >= 4.08 V below the U5 turn-off minimum); the input qualification is the U5 UVLO. Arming timelines (cold start at the worst loaded 20 V minimum, slow PD contract, brown-out after/inside the window, overload chatter, hot plug into a live bus, load release, U20 guard before ARMED, short RESET) pass R1-R4; the S8.4 wiring fails them (regression test)."
    },
    {
      "item": "C-hash",
      "change": "Review record hashes only files a clean clone has: the git-ignored *.kicad_prl files are no longer hashed and the local tests log / check directory (research/, git-ignored) are recorded by path only."
    },
    {
      "item": "C-status",
      "change": "MAIN_LED_OK = MAIN_OK AND V20_OK now means \"U5 on with valid FLT/PGOOD\"; ANY_BAD = NOT(MAIN_LED_OK AND P12_OK AND P5_OK AND N12_OK). Notes, page texts and the fault matrix say so."
    },
    {
      "item": "C-POR",
      "change": "Replug / power-on-reset race of the U20 -12V channel (R100/C67 loaded by R98, TPS3808 >= 12 ms POR): calcs replug_por, nominal 9.5 ms, worst 13.75 ms: margin NOT established, explicit OPEN item. The S8.4 ~1 ms margin (v3v3_loss) ignored the R98 load and is withdrawn."
    },
    {
      "item": "kept",
      "change": "Every S8.4 decision unchanged: U23 TPS259470ARPWR with R108/TP21 (P5_FLT_N), OVLO R107/R101/R102, ILM R103/R104, C68, R11/R12 0.1 %, U18/U20 on VPD, local-loop contract, 2.0 A +5V rating, mask webs, -12V start-up, sourcing decision and mechanical records. The crowbar-vs-eFuse question stays open."
    }
  ],
